# hw definition for a custom Holybro Kakute F4 Wing variant that adds a
# hardware ToneAlarm (tone) buzzer on the addressable-LED ("LED") pad.
#
# The stock Kakute F4 Wing defines no buzzer at all, so ArduPilot tunes
# (arming, GPS lock, auto-takeoff/launch cues, failsafe) otherwise only
# beep through the DShot ESCs. This variant repurposes the WS2812 "LED"
# strip pad - PA1, the board's default servo output 7 / NeoPixel - as a
# hardware tone buzzer.
#
# PA1 is remapped from TIM5_CH2 to TIM2_CH2 and marked ALARM. That defines
# HAL_PWM_ALARM, so AP_ToneAlarm plays pitched tunes on a passive buzzer
# wired to the LED pad. TIM2 is unused elsewhere on this board (PWM outputs
# use TIM1/3/5/8, the system timer is TIM9), so no motor PWM group is
# affected.
#
# Cost: the addressable LED-strip output on the "LED" pad is given up for
# the buzzer. The onboard PC5 status LED is unaffected, and no M1-M6
# motor/servo output is lost.
#
# Board ID is inherited (Holybro-KakuteF4-Wing) so this flashes over the
# stock bootloader like a normal firmware update. Wire a *passive* buzzer
# to the LED pad (signal -> transistor -> buzzer, powered from 5V/GND);
# see Readme.md.

include ../KakuteF4-Wing/hwdef.dat

# repurpose the WS2812 "LED" pad (PA1) as a tone buzzer on a free timer.
# TIM2 is unused elsewhere on this board, so the PWM groups (TIM1/3/5/8)
# and the system timer (TIM9) are unaffected.
undef PA1
PA1 TIM2_CH2 TIM2 GPIO(56) ALARM
